text:
Wave 3 is now 6 of 15 tickets landed. The latest two are TKA-0069 (`5368b96`, all app data kept out of backup and device transfer) and TKA-0009 (`cba6b9a`, the Toggl API client). The client builds exactly one `OkHttpClient`, which I checked in the source, and its sitting reported 27 JVM tests passing.

The next sitting on the app track has started. It covers the network security config (TKA-0010), the real-Tokkl-server test harness (TKA-0006) and keystore storage for the API token (TKA-0011). It will:
- bind the Tokkl container's port to 127.0.0.1 only, so the seeded test account isn't reachable from your LAN or tailnet;
- leave the four ddev containers alone;
- remove its own container and volume when it finishes, including after a failed test run;
- shut the emulator and adb down at the end.

The parsing port (TKA-0012) has committed on its branch and is finishing its report.
